      "value": "@{5af5f97d56feb85f40086953|full_name}: Depends on the count. I have a 60K poly model that lags a ton with no Dynamic Bones if any Shape Keys are used on it. This means if someone uses it to talk (Visemes) frames jump from 90 to 45 even if you're just alone in a world with a single directional real-time light. Meanwhile decimating it down to 40K for some magical reason lets everything work fine with both Blend Shapes and Dynamic Bones, literally just swapping the mesh out for one with 33% fewer polygons. I don't understand this at all, I assume it hit some kind of limit or wall that pushed it over the edge into being horrible.\n\nThat said, yeah, polygons without animators affecting them don't really matter.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
